"""Build scene.blend from scratch (reproducible scene construction).

    blender --background --python build_scene.py

Requires (build time only; the finished scene.blend needs neither):
  * the MPFB add-on (MakeHuman Plugin For Blender, GPL code / CC0 assets) enabled in Blender
  * the CC0 MakeHuman system asset pack unzipped into assets/mh_assets/
  * textures/ generated by tools/make_textures.py (iris, sclera) and tools/bake_skin.py (skin)

What it does
  1. Creates the MakeHuman base human (metres), bakes the shape, adds the default rig,
     eyebrows and eyelashes.
  2. Detects the eye centres, the face forward axis F and up axis U from the model.
  3. Re-seats the eye.L / eye.R bones so each pivots exactly at its eyeball centre with its
     Y axis along F, and parents a purpose-built eyeball (sclera + iris + pupil + refractive
     cornea shell) to each bone.
  4. Places the fixation target (M + 0.35 F), the locked camera (M + 0.40 F) and constant
     studio lighting; fixes all render settings (1024x1024, Cycles, fixed seed).
  5. Stores the calibration as JSON in scene["xr_calib"], packs textures, saves scene.blend.
"""
import importlib
import json
import math
import os
import sys

import bmesh
import bpy
from mathutils import Matrix, Vector

